msgid "These tutorials will guide you through building applications using the AT Protocol. Each tutorial focuses on a specific use case or feature, providing step-by-step instructions and code examples.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/tutorials/en.mdx:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our tutorials are organized to be completed in order, but each tutorial is self-contained and can be followed independently.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/tutorials/en.mdx:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Note>\n"
"These tutorials are written to be cross-platform. In general, we recommend using platforms supported by [homebrew](https://brew.sh/): macOS, Linux, or [WSL](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/) on Windows. There is also an outstanding [DNS bug](https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/62347) affecting Node.js on Windows when not using WSL, which can break `lex` resolution.\n"
"</Note>\n"
msgstr ""

